<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Przemysław of Racibórz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1258–1306</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Przemysław (c. 1258–1306) was a Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>, the first ruler of the separate duchy created when the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-of-opole">Władysław of Opole</a> divided their father's lands in 1281. He was succeeded by his son Leszek, the last duke of the line, while his daughter Anna married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii-of-opava">Nicholas II of Opava</a>, who later inherited the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/przemyslaw-of-raciborz.jpg" alt="Przemysław of Racibórz" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: project: Leszek Ołdak, Marian Panic, Bolesław Polnar, vectorization: Poznaniak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POL_wojew%C3%B3dztwo_opolskie_COA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
